   805→  - _ulid: 01KFQ84FVYMN3Z0HXWZ5AK7CQD
   806→    slugs:
   807→      - multi-directory-daemon
   808→    title: Multi-Directory Daemon Architecture
   809→    type: feature
   810→    tags:
   811→      - daemon
   812→      - architecture
   813→      - multi-project
   814→    description: |
   815→      Extends the daemon server to support multiple kspec projects simultaneously from a single
   816→      daemon process. Projects are identified via X-Kspec-Dir HTTP header. Enables E2E testing
   817→      with isolated fixtures and multi-project development workflows.
   818→
   819→      Key architectural changes:
   820→      - Global daemon with PID/port files at ~/.config/kspec/
   821→      - Project context caching with on-demand registration
   822→      - Per-project file watchers
   823→      - WebSocket connections bound to specific projects
   824→
   825→      BREAKING CHANGE: PID/port files move from .kspec/.daemon.pid to ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid
   826→    depends_on:
   827→      - "@daemon-server"
   828→      - "@api-contract"
   829→    implements: []
   830→    relates_to:
   831→      - "@cli-serve-commands"
   832→    tests: []
   833→    traits:
   834→      - "@trait-localhost-security"
   835→      - "@trait-websocket-protocol"
   836→    notes:
   837→      - _ulid: 01KFQ84FVZB2CWH7Y4GPQR8M9N
   838→        created_at: 2026-01-24T06:00:00.000Z
   839→        author: "@claude"
   840→        content: |
   841→          Design decisions:
   842→          - X-Kspec-Dir header for project selection (clean URLs, easy for clients)
   843→          - Single bundled web UI (consistent version across projects)
   844→          - On-demand project registration (auto-register on first request)
   845→          - No memory limit on cached projects (keep until restart)
   846→          - Global PID at ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid
   847→          - Per-project file watchers
   848→          - Backwards compatible (no header = startup cwd project if valid)
   849→    created: 2026-01-24T06:00:00.000Z
   850→    acceptance_criteria:
   851→      - id: ac-1
   852→        given: daemon is running
   853→        when: request includes X-Kspec-Dir header with valid absolute path
   854→        then: daemon uses that project's context for the request
   855→      - id: ac-2
   856→        given: daemon started from directory with .kspec/
   857→        when: request has no X-Kspec-Dir header
   858→        then: daemon uses startup directory's project as default
   859→      - id: ac-3
   860→        given: daemon started from directory without .kspec/
   861→        when: request without X-Kspec-Dir arrives
   862→        then: return 400 with error "No default project configured. Specify X-Kspec-Dir header."
   863→      - id: ac-4
   864→        given: request specifies unknown project path
   865→        when: path is valid kspec project
   866→        then: daemon auto-registers and caches project context
   867→      - id: ac-5
   868→        given: request specifies invalid path (no .kspec/)
   869→        when: request processed
   870→        then: return 400 with error "Invalid kspec project - .kspec/ not found at <path>"
   871→      - id: ac-6
   872→        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value
   873→        when: path is relative
   874→        then: reject with 400 and error "Path must be absolute"
   875→      - id: ac-7
   876→        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value
   877→        when: path contains ".." segments
   878→        then: reject with 400 and error "Path must not contain parent traversal"
   879→      - id: ac-8
   880→        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value
   881→        when: normalized path differs from provided path
   882→        then: use normalized path for registration (resolve "." segments, remove trailing slashes, do NOT
   883→          resolve symlinks)
   884→      - id: ac-8b
   885→        given: X-Kspec-Dir points to path with insufficient read permissions
   886→        when: request processed
   887→        then: return 403 with error "Permission denied - cannot read <path>"
   888→      - id: ac-9
   889→        given: no daemon running
   890→        when: kspec serve start runs from any directory
   891→        then: daemon starts and writes PID to ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid and port to
   892→          ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port
   893→      - id: ac-9b
   894→        given: ~/.config/kspec/ does not exist
   895→        when: daemon starts
   896→        then: create directory with mode 0755 before writing PID/port files
   897→      - id: ac-9c
   898→        given: ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port exists but contains invalid content
   899→        when: CLI reads port
   900→        then: return error "Invalid daemon port file" and suggest "kspec serve stop && kspec serve start"
   901→      - id: ac-10
   902→        given: daemon running on port 3456
   903→        when: kspec serve start runs from different directory
   904→        then: command exits with success and outputs "Daemon already running on port 3456" (no second
   905→          instance started)
   906→      - id: ac-10b
   907→        given: two kspec serve start commands run concurrently (neither has written PID yet)
   908→        when: both check for running daemon
   909→        then: only one daemon starts (use file lock on PID file)
   910→      - id: ac-11
   911→        given: daemon running
   912→        when: kspec serve stop runs from any directory
   913→        then: daemon stops and removes global PID and port files
   914→      - id: ac-12
   915→        given: daemon running
   916→        when: kspec serve status runs
   917→        then: shows daemon status with port, uptime, and list of registered projects with their paths
   918→      - id: ac-13
   919→        given: CLI needs to connect to daemon
   920→        when: daemon is running
   921→        then: CLI reads port from ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port
   922→      - id: ac-14
   923→        given: daemon restarts
   924→        when: first request for a project arrives
   925→        then: project is re-registered automatically (same as initial registration)
   926→      - id: ac-15
   927→        given: daemon running with registered projects
   928→        when: daemon restarts
   929→        then: registered project list is empty (no persistence across restarts)
   930→      - id: ac-16
   931→        given: two concurrent requests for unregistered project with same path
   932→        when: processed
   933→        then: both succeed and share the same registered project context (no duplicate watchers)
   934→      - id: ac-17
   935→        given: project is registered
   936→        when: files change in project's .kspec/
   937→        then: file watcher triggers events scoped to that project
   938→      - id: ac-18
   939→        given: multiple projects registered
   940→        when: Project A changes
   941→        then: only Project A's WebSocket subscribers receive updates
   942→      - id: ac-19
   943→        given: project watcher creation fails due to OS limits (ulimit)
   944→        when: error occurs
   945→        then: project registration fails with 503 and error "Unable to watch project - resource limit
   946→          reached"
   947→      - id: ac-20
   948→        given: registered project's .kspec/ directory is deleted
   949→        when: next request arrives for that project
   950→        then: return 404 and unregister project automatically
   951→      - id: ac-21
   952→        given: WebSocket client connects with X-Kspec-Dir header during handshake
   953→        when: connection established
   954→        then: connection is bound to that project for its lifetime and only receives events from that
   955→          project
   956→      - id: ac-21b
   957→        given: WebSocket connection is established and bound to project
   958→        when: client attempts to change project
   959→        then: project binding is immutable - client must disconnect and reconnect with new header
   960→      - id: ac-22
   961→        given: WebSocket client connects without X-Kspec-Dir header
   962→        when: default project exists
   963→        then: connection is bound to default project
   964→      - id: ac-23
   965→        given: WebSocket client connects without X-Kspec-Dir header
   966→        when: no default project
   967→        then: connection is rejected with close code 4000 and reason "No project specified"
   968→      - id: ac-24
   969→        given: multi-project mode
   970→        when: any API endpoint is called
   971→        then: response data is scoped to the request's project (no cross-project data leakage)
   972→      - id: ac-25
   973→        given: web UI loads
   974→        when: more than one project registered
   975→        then: project selector is shown listing all registered projects
   976→      - id: ac-26
   977→        given: user selects project in UI
   978→        when: selection changes
   979→        then: all subsequent API requests include that project's path in X-Kspec-Dir header
   980→      - id: ac-27
   981→        given: UI is showing project data
   982→        when: different project selected
   983→        then: UI reloads data from newly selected project
   984→      - id: ac-28
   985→        given: GET /api/projects
   986→        when: called
   987→        then: returns list of registered projects with paths, registration time, and watcher status
   988→      - id: ac-29
   989→        given: POST /api/projects
   990→        when: called with {path string} body
   991→        then: manually registers a project (for explicit registration use cases)
   992→      - id: ac-30
   993→        given: DELETE /api/projects/:encodedPath
   994→        when: called
   995→        then: unregisters project and stops its file watcher
   996→      - id: ac-8c
   997→        given: X-Kspec-Dir header contains symlinked path
   998→        when: path resolves to same directory as another registered project via symlink
   999→        then: paths are treated as separate projects (symlinks are NOT resolved during normalization)
  1000→      - id: ac-20b
  1001→        given: daemon started from directory with .kspec/ which is later deleted
  1002→        when: request without X-Kspec-Dir arrives after default project .kspec/ deleted
  1003→        then: return 400 with error 'Default project no longer valid. Specify X-Kspec-Dir header.'
  1004→      - id: ac-11b
  1005→        given: daemon is shutting down
  1006→        when: shutdown signal received
  1007→        then: all project watchers are stopped and all WebSocket connections are closed before process exits
  1008→    status:
  1009→      maturity: draft
  1010→      implementation: implemented
